<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="a" from="1/4" to="1/2" step="1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="b" from="1/2" to="3/2" step="1/4" exclude="4*$a"/>

  <function name="v" variable="t">$b - $a*t</function>
  <function name="s" variable="t">$b*t - $a*t^2/2</function>

  <styleDefinition styleNumber="10"
    fillColor="#FFFFFF"
    fillOpacity="1"
    lineColor="#FFFFFF"
    />

</setup>

<p>
  Suppose that a moving object for times <m>t = 0</m> to <m>t = 8</m> (seconds) has its velocity is given by the function 
  <me>
    v(t) = $v
  </me>
  with units feet per second.  A graph of <m>v</m> is provided below; note that the vertical and horizontal scales are different.
</p>

      <graph grid="true" size="medium" xMin="-0.25" xMax="8.25" yMin="$b-$a*8-1" yMax="$b+1" fixAxes="true" showNavigation="false">
        <shortDescription>a graph of the function v on the interval t equals 0 to t equals 8</shortDescription>
        $v
        <label fixed anchor="(0.4,$b+0.7)">ft/sec</label>
        <label fixed anchor="(7.5,0.1)">sec</label>
        <rectangle fixed center="($b/$a+0.2,0.25)" width="0.5" height="0.25" filled styleNumber="10"></rectangle>
        <label fixed anchor="($b/$a+0.2,0.25)"><m>v(t)</m></label>
      </graph>
<p>
  Use the graph and the formula for <m>v(t)</m> to determine each of the following quantities.
</p>
<p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <p>
        The object's <answer><label>change in position on <m>[0, <math simplify>$b/$a</math>]</m> is</label>$$s($b/$a)</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        The object's <answer><label>change in position on <m>[<math simplify>$b/$a</math>, 8]</m> is </label>$$s(8)-$$s($b/$a)</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        The object's <answer><label>total change in position on <m>[0, 8]</m> is </label>$$s(8)-$$s(0)</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        The object's <answer><label>total distance traveled on <m>[0, 8]</m> is </label>2*$$s($b/$a) - $$s(8)</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</p>
<p>
  The units on each of the quantities found above are 
        <answer><choiceInput inline><shortDescription>options for units</shortDescription>
          <choice>?</choice>
          <choice>feet per second</choice>
          <choice>seconds</choice>
          <choice credit="1">feet</choice>
        </choiceInput></answer>.
</p>
